  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rEXISTING LOCATION & BLOCK PLANS - 2301/PP/201\rEXISTING BASEMENT & GROUND PLANS - 2301/PP2/202 Rev C\rEXISTING ROOF PLAN - 2301/PP2/203 Rev B \rEXISTING ELEVATIONS - 2301/PP2/104 Rev B\rEXISTING A-A SECTION 2301/BC/106 - Rev A\r\rEnergy Statement \rHeritage Statement \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Notwithstanding condition no. 2 above, within two months of the date of this permission, revised plans which correlate, showing the side window on the west elevation shall be submitted and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: These details have not been submitted and to ensure that all plans correlate.",
    "Within two months of the date of this permissision, details of all new means of enclosure shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.  The development shall be completed, within four months of the date of this permission,  in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: In the interests of visual amenity and public safety.",
    "Within two months of the date of the permission, a scheme of landscaping shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.  The approved landscaping scheme shall be implemented within four months of the date of the permission and photographic evidence submitted within four months.\r\rReason: To ensure the satisfactory provision of private amenity space and in the interests of biodiversity.",
    "Within two months of the date of this permission, details of the secure and covered cycle parking spaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be completed, within four months of the permission and such facilities to be retained for the lifetime of the development\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of cycle parking in line with the Council's adopted standards\r\r",
    "Within two months of the date of this permission, details of storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be completed, within four months of the permission and such facilities to be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets."
  ],
